# QuickBite – MERN Food Delivery Website

A full-stack food ordering platform built with MongoDB, Express, React and Node.js, featuring online payments, coupons, ratings and a complete admin panel.

| App | Description | Tech | URL |
|---|---|---|---|
| backend/ | REST API | Node.js, Express, MongoDB (Mongoose) | http://localhost:4000 |
| frontend/ | Customer website | React, Vite | http://localhost:5173 |
| admin/ | Admin panel | React, Vite | http://localhost:5174 |

## Features

### Customer
- Browse the menu by category, search dishes, view dish details and reviews
- Cart that works before login and syncs to the account after sign-in
- Secure sign-up and login (JWT authentication, bcrypt password hashing)
- Checkout with delivery address, coupon codes, card payment or Cash on Delivery
- Order tracking with live status
- Cancel orders with automatic refund
- Ratings and reviews for delivered dishes

### Admin
- Secure admin login
- Add and remove dishes with image upload (Multer)
- Manage orders and update status (Processing → Out for Delivery → Delivered / Cancelled)
- Dashboard with total orders, pending orders and revenue
- Create and manage coupons (flat or percentage, minimum order, usage limit, expiry)
- Moderate customer reviews

### Security
- Prices and discounts are calculated on the server
- Payments are verified on the server before an order is confirmed
- Admin-only routes are protected by role-based tokens

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: React, React Router, Context API, Axios, Vite
- Backend: Node.js, Express.js, Mongoose, JWT, bcrypt, Multer
- Database: MongoDB (built-in local instance or MongoDB Atlas)
- Payments: Stripe Checkout and a built-in test-mode card payment

## Getting Started

Requirement: Node.js 18 or newer. No database setup is needed; the backend starts a local MongoDB automatically.

```bash
# Terminal 1: Backend
cd backend
npm install
npm run server

# Terminal 2: Customer website
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev

# Terminal 3: Admin panel
cd admin
npm install
npm run dev
```

- Sample dishes and coupons are added on the first start
- Run `npm run photos` in the backend folder to download real food photos
- Admin login: `admin@quickbite.com` / `admin12345`
- Test card: `4242 4242 4242 4242`, any future date, any CVC
- Sample coupons: `WELCOME50` (₹50 off above ₹199), `FEAST20` (20% off above ₹300)

## Configuration (optional)

Create `backend/.env` from `.env.example` to change the defaults:

- `MONGO_URL` – use MongoDB Atlas instead of the local database
- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` – enable Stripe Checkout
- `ADMIN_EMAIL`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD` – admin login
- `JWT_SECRET` – token signing secret (set before deployment)

## Project Structure

```
quickbite/
├── backend/    config, models, controllers, routes, middleware, scripts
├── frontend/   React customer app (components, pages, context)
└── admin/      React admin panel (pages, components)
```

## Main API Endpoints
- Food: `GET /api/food/list`, `POST /api/food/add`, `POST /api/food/remove`
- Auth: `POST /api/user/register`, `POST /api/user/login`, `POST /api/admin/login`
- Cart: `GET /api/cart/get`, `POST /api/cart/add`, `POST /api/cart/remove`
- Orders: `POST /api/order/place`, `GET /api/order/userorders`, `POST /api/order/cancel`, `POST /api/order/status`
- Coupons: `POST /api/coupon/apply`, `POST /api/coupon/add`, `GET /api/coupon/list`
- Reviews: `GET /api/review/food/:foodId`, `POST /api/review/add`

## Future Scope
- Razorpay and UPI payments
- Live delivery tracking on a map
- Email and SMS notifications
- Cloud image storage and deployment
